// Cardnull OS 2 — the USB stick in the running system
// (Stone 43).
//
// Every other USB road in this system is ears: the two
// keyboard drivers (usbkey.nifla on the UHCI road,
// xhcikey.nifla on the xHCI road) listen, and the
// firmware's own road (Stone 17) boots the system off a
// stick but hands the running system nothing. This
// library is the running system's own hands on a USB
// stick: it raises a mass-storage device standing on
// the xHCI bus, speaks the bulk-only transport the
// sticks of the world speak (a command wrapper out,
// the data, a status wrapper back), and reads and
// writes the stick's sectors with the SCSI words the
// transport carries (READ(10), WRITE(10), READ
// CAPACITY, TEST UNIT READY, SYNCHRONIZE CACHE).
//
// The controller is shared with the xHCI keyboard
// road, and shared honestly: the command ring, the
// event ring, and the device-place list are the
// controller's own, kept in that road's desk, and this
// library uses them through that road's own hands
// (xcmd, xbell, xnextevt) exactly as the keyboard's
// waking does. The stick's own estate — its ledger,
// its contexts, its three rings (control, bulk out,
// bulk in), its data ground — lives in that same desk,
// on ground the keyboard road never touches: above
// every field its building lays (its scratch pages
// included, whose count its ledger keeps), page-lined,
// with the ground's place kept at the one ledger place
// its road left free (252). Every word below therefore
// takes the one desk, as the keyboard road's words do,
// and reads the stick's ledger through the two small
// hands sg and sp, which reckon from the ground. The
// main body takes the desk larger for this stone
// (98304 bytes) so the ground stands clear at every
// alignment. The raising walks the ports the
// keyboard's raising left alone: the keyboard's own
// port is skipped by its number, and the keyboard
// road's ledger places this walk borrows (its port
// and speed) are handed back as they were found, so
// the keyboard stands exactly as it stood.
//
// The stick, once raised, can carry the system's
// keeping — the settings card, the notes page, the
// kept picture — in the very layout diskkeep.nifla
// lays on a hard disk (its heading tells the layout
// whole): this library's second half is that layout's
// twin on the stick, word for word, so the main body
// chooses at its rising which disk keeps its memory
// and the keeping itself never knows the difference.
// The choice is the main body's, and its rule is
// plain: a fitted hard disk keeps its place, as it
// always has; the stick keeps the memory when no hard
// disk stands fitted. The setup gate's discipline is
// the twins' too: nothing is written to a stick the
// gate has not given over, and the giving-over
// (udisksetup) clears and cards the stick exactly as
// disksetup does a hard disk.
//
// Honest bounds, said once here: transfers are whole
// sectors of 512 bytes, one at a time, and a stick
// whose sector is not 512 bytes is refused at the
// raising. A transfer is short — the reckonings here
// are done in the asking, not in a background — but
// while one runs, this library reads the controller's
// event ring, and a keyboard report landing in that
// same moment may be set aside unread: a key pressed
// in the very instant of a keeping write may ask a
// second press. The stick is raised once, at the
// rising; a stick plugged in later is not seen until
// the next rising, as no road in this system yet
// watches for arrivals.
//
// Stone 50 gives this library a third part, after the
// transport and the keeping: the system itself, from
// the stick. A stick made from the system's image
// (Stone 17: the disc's own bytes, with the master
// boot record at its head) carries the whole system,
// and the makings at this file's end let the running
// system lay that system onto the computer's own hard
// disk — the image copied sector by sector to the
// disk's ground past the keeping (the main body names
// the beginning), proved at three of its places, and
// the disk's own boot record laid last of all, from
// the stick's record with its partition table's
// beginning set to where the image now stands. The
// stick is only ever read by these makings: an
// installing never writes its source.

// ---- the stick's ledger ----
//
// The ledger stands at the ground's head (the ground
// itself is reckoned by ubuild and kept at the desk's
// place 252); its places, reckoned from the ground:
//
//   0   the stick's standing: 0 untouched, 1 raised
//       and ready, 2 no stick stands on the bus,
//       255 a stick answered but could not be raised
//   4   the port the stick stands on
//   8   the stick's place (its slot) with the
//       controller
//   12  the stick's speed, in the controller's own
//       reckoning (1 full, 2 low, 3 high, 4 super)
//   16  the control door's packet bound
//   20  the bulk-in door's number (its place in the
//       device, without the direction bit)
//   24  the bulk-in door's packet bound
//   28  the bulk-in door's place in the controller's
//       reckoning (its DCI: door * 2 + 1)
//   32  the bulk-out door's number
//   36  the bulk-out door's packet bound
//   40  the bulk-out door's place (its DCI: door * 2)
//   44  how many sectors the stick holds
//   48  the command wrapper's mark, growing by one
//       with every command carried
//   52  the control ring's standing, 56 its cycle
//   60  the bulk-out ring's standing, 64 its cycle
//   68  the bulk-in ring's standing, 72 its cycle
//   76  the input context's place in the desk
//   80  the output context's place
//   84  the control ring's place
//   88  the bulk-out ring's place
//   92  the bulk-in ring's place
//   96  the data ground's place: 4096 bytes of
//       transfer ground, then the command wrapper's
//       room at +4096, the status wrapper's room at
//       +4608, and the command's own room at +5120
//   100 the setup packet's room's place
//   104 the last transfer event's unbrought remainder
//   220 the transfer block staging (four words), the
//       same shape the xHCI road stages at its own
//       220 — kept here because the ring hand reads
//       the staging from the desk it is handed, and
//       the stick's rings are laid from this ledger's
//       reckoning of their places
//
// The regions stand from the ground's +256: the input
// context (4224 bytes), the output context (4224),
// the control ring (1024), the bulk-out ring (1024),
// the bulk-in ring (1024), the data ground (8192),
// and the setup room (64) — the estate ends at the
// ground's +20032.

// Reads one of the stick's ledger words, reckoned
// from the ground kept at the desk's place 252.
make sg(desk: bytes, off: number) -> number {
    give get32(desk, get32(desk, 252) + off)
}

// Lays one of the stick's ledger words.
make sp(desk: bytes, off: number, value: number) {
    put32(desk, get32(desk, 252) + off, value)
}

// Lays the stick's estate: the ground reckoned from
// the keyboard road's own building — above its fields
// (whose last, its scratch pages, end at its base +
// 29632 + its scratch count's pages, the count kept
// at its 240) — and lined to a page; the ground's
// place kept at the desk's 252; the regions' places
// laid in the ledger; and the rings' standings at
// their openings.
make ubuild(desk: bytes) {
    let b = get32(desk, 32)
    let end = b + 29632 + get32(desk, 240) * 4096
    let g = end - (end / 4096) * 4096
    if g != 0 {
        g = 4096 - g
    }
    let ground = end + g
    put32(desk, 252, ground)
    sp(desk, 76, ground + 256)
    sp(desk, 80, ground + 4480)
    sp(desk, 84, ground + 8704)
    sp(desk, 88, ground + 9728)
    sp(desk, 92, ground + 10752)
    sp(desk, 96, ground + 11776)
    sp(desk, 100, ground + 19968)
    sp(desk, 52, 0)
    sp(desk, 56, 1)
    sp(desk, 60, 0)
    sp(desk, 64, 1)
    sp(desk, 68, 0)
    sp(desk, 72, 1)
    sp(desk, 48, 0)
}

// Stages one transfer block's four words in the
// stick's ledger (at its 220), for the ring hand
// below (uenq) to lay into one of the stick's rings.
make ustage(desk: bytes, d0: number, d1: number, d2: number, d3: number) {
    sp(desk, 220, d0)
    sp(desk, 224, d1)
    sp(desk, 228, d2)
    sp(desk, 232, d3)
}

// Lays the staged block into one of the stick's
// rings, doing the xHCI road's ring hand's (xenq's)
// own work in the stick's reckoning — the staging and
// the standings read from the stick's ledger, the
// ring laid in the desk where it stands: the block
// at the standing's place with the ring's cycle in
// its fourth word, and at the ring's last usable
// place (62 of 64) a link block laid behind it —
// pointing home, its toggle raised — and the
// standing wrapped home with its cycle turned,
// exactly as xenq lays for the keyboard's rings.
make uenq(desk: bytes, ring: number, idxoff: number, cycoff: number) {
    let idx = sg(desk, idxoff)
    let cyc = sg(desk, cycoff)
    let at = ring + idx * 16
    put32(desk, at, sg(desk, 220))
    put32(desk, at + 4, sg(desk, 224))
    put32(desk, at + 8, sg(desk, 228))
    put32(desk, at + 12, sg(desk, 232) + cyc)
    if idx == 62 {
        let lat = ring + 63 * 16
        put32(desk, lat, xphys(desk, ring))
        put32(desk, lat + 4, 0)
        put32(desk, lat + 8, 0)
        put32(desk, lat + 12, cyc + 2 + 6 * 1024)
        sp(desk, idxoff, 0)
        sp(desk, cycoff, 1 - cyc)
    } else {
        sp(desk, idxoff, idx + 1)
    }
}

// Waits for the answering event of the transfer now
// outstanding on one of the stick's doors — the
// transfer kind (32) for the stick's place and that
// door — setting every other event aside, the
// keyboard's own included (see the heading's honest
// bounds). Gives back the completion code, or -1 when
// none came in five seconds; the event's unbrought
// remainder is kept at the stick ledger's 104.
make uwaitep(desk: bytes, dci: number) -> number {
    let deadline = ticks() + 500
    while ticks() < deadline {
        if xnextevt(desk) == 1 {
            if xevtype(desk) == 32 {
                if andmask(get32(desk, 196) / 16777216, 255) == sg(desk, 8) {
                    if andmask(get32(desk, 196) / 65536, 31) == dci {
                        sp(desk, 104, andmask(get32(desk, 192), 16777215))
                        give xevcode(desk)
                    }
                }
            }
            // The keyboard's completions share this ring;
            // meeting one here, keep the keyboard's
            // service on its behalf (see xkbkeep in the
            // keyboard's library), never pass it by.
            xkbkeep(desk)
        } else {
            waittick()
        }
    }
    give 0 - 1
}

// ---- the control road, the stick's own ----

// Stages a control conversation's opening packet in
// the stick's own setup room, in two calls, as the
// xHCI road's staging does for the keyboard.
make ustagesetup1(desk: bytes, rt: number, req: number, value: number) {
    let o = sg(desk, 100)
    desk[o] = rt
    desk[o + 1] = req
    desk[o + 2] = lobyte(value)
    desk[o + 3] = hibyte(value)
}

make ustagesetup2(desk: bytes, index: number, length: number) {
    let o = sg(desk, 100)
    desk[o + 4] = lobyte(index)
    desk[o + 5] = hibyte(index)
    desk[o + 6] = lobyte(length)
    desk[o + 7] = hibyte(length)
}

// One control conversation, whole, on the stick's
// control ring — the xHCI road's xcontrol reckoned
// again for this estate: a setup block carrying its
// packet in itself, the data block when there is one
// (its ground the data ground's head), and the status
// block closing it, its direction the opposite of the
// data's. Comes home with the data's true count, or
// -1 when the conversation did not complete in
// success or in an honest short answer.
make ucontrol(desk: bytes, hasdata: number, inward: number, datalen: number) -> number {
    let s = sg(desk, 100)
    let trt = 0
    if hasdata == 1 {
        trt = 2
        if inward == 1 {
            trt = 3
        }
    }
    ustage(desk, get32(desk, s), get32(desk, s + 4), 8, 2 * 1024 + 64 + trt * 65536)
    uenq(desk, sg(desk, 84), 52, 56)
    if hasdata == 1 {
        let dd3 = 3 * 1024 + 16
        if inward == 1 {
            dd3 = dd3 + 4 + 65536
        }
        ustage(desk, xphys(desk, sg(desk, 96)), 0, datalen, dd3)
        uenq(desk, sg(desk, 84), 52, 56)
    }
    let sdir = 1
    if hasdata == 1 {
        sdir = 1 - inward
    }
    ustage(desk, 0, 0, 0, 4 * 1024 + 32 + sdir * 65536)
    uenq(desk, sg(desk, 84), 52, 56)
    xbell(desk, sg(desk, 8), 1)
    let code = uwaitep(desk, 1)
    if code == 1 {
        if hasdata == 1 {
            give datalen - sg(desk, 104)
        }
        give 0
    }
    if code == 13 {
        if hasdata == 1 {
            if inward == 1 {
                give datalen - sg(desk, 104)
            }
        }
    }
    give 0 - 1
}

// Asks for a description at the stick's place: the
// standard asking (number 6), with the kind in the
// value's high byte. The bytes land at the data
// ground's head; the true count comes home.
make ugetdesc(desk: bytes, kind: number, len: number) -> number {
    ustagesetup1(desk, 128, 6, kind * 256)
    ustagesetup2(desk, 0, len)
    give ucontrol(desk, 1, 1, len)
}

// ---- the raising ----

// Lays the input context for addressing the stick:
// its place's context (its speed and its root port,
// one door reckoned so far) and the control door's
// context (its error allowance, its kind, its packet
// bound, and its ring, whose reading opens at the
// first cycle) — the xHCI road's xlayaddress reckoned
// for this estate, with the controller's place list
// told where the stick's output context stands.
make ulayaddress(desk: bytes) {
    // The stick's control ring is shared by every
    // waking this library makes (a device of another
    // kind may be woken and set aside before the stick
    // is found), and the door laid below is told the
    // ring from its head at the first cycle — so the
    // ring is scrubbed clean and the laying hand stood
    // at the head too, first cycle, before the laying:
    // the same law the keyboard road keeps (see
    // xlayaddress there), and for the same reason: the
    // controller reads ahead while the reckoning bit
    // matches, and a former waking's leavings would be
    // carried out as this device's own askings.
    xzero(desk, sg(desk, 84), 1024)
    sp(desk, 52, 0)
    sp(desk, 56, 1)
    let inp = sg(desk, 76)
    let cs = get32(desk, 208)
    xzero(desk, inp, 4224)
    xzero(desk, sg(desk, 80), 4224)
    put32(desk, inp + 4, 3)
    put32(desk, inp + cs, sg(desk, 12) * 1048576 + 268435456)
    put32(desk, inp + cs + 4, sg(desk, 4) * 65536)
    put32(desk, inp + cs * 2 + 4, 6 + 32 + sg(desk, 16) * 65536)
    put32(desk, inp + cs * 2 + 8, xphys(desk, sg(desk, 84)) + 1)
    put32(desk, inp + cs * 2 + 16, 8)
    let dcbaa = get32(desk, 156)
    let slot = sg(desk, 8)
    put32(desk, dcbaa + slot * 8, xphys(desk, sg(desk, 80)))
    put32(desk, dcbaa + slot * 8 + 4, 0)
}

// Raises the stick standing on one port whose reset
// has already been made and whose speed stands in
// this ledger: a place from the controller, the
// device addressed, its description read and its
// control door's true bound learned, its whole
// arrangement read and searched for the mass-storage
// face (class 8, the SCSI words, the bulk-only
// carriage) with its two bulk doors, those doors
// arranged with the controller, and the arrangement
// set. Comes home with the verdict: 2 — it did not
// answer its waking; 3 — it answered, and declared
// another kind; 4 — a stick, arranged and ready for
// the transport below.
make uwake(desk: bytes) -> number {
    let d = sg(desk, 96)
    if xcmd(desk, 9, 0, 0, 0) != 1 {
        give 2
    }
    sp(desk, 8, get32(desk, 200))
    if sg(desk, 8) < 1 {
        give 2
    }
    let guess = 64
    if sg(desk, 12) == 2 {
        guess = 8
    }
    if sg(desk, 12) == 4 {
        guess = 512
    }
    sp(desk, 16, guess)
    ulayaddress(desk)
    if xcmd(desk, 11, xphys(desk, sg(desk, 76)), 0, sg(desk, 8)) != 1 {
        give 2
    }
    usbwait(1)
    if ugetdesc(desk, 1, 8) < 8 {
        give 2
    }
    let real = desk[d + 7]
    if real != guess {
        if real >= 8 {
            sp(desk, 16, real)
            let inp = sg(desk, 76)
            let cs = get32(desk, 208)
            xzero(desk, inp, 4224)
            put32(desk, inp + 4, 2)
            put32(desk, inp + cs * 2 + 4, 6 + 32 + real * 65536)
            put32(desk, inp + cs * 2 + 8, xphys(desk, sg(desk, 84)) + 1)
            put32(desk, inp + cs * 2 + 16, 8)
            if xcmd(desk, 13, xphys(desk, inp), 0, sg(desk, 8)) != 1 {
                give 2
            }
        }
    }
    if ugetdesc(desk, 1, 18) < 18 {
        give 2
    }
    if ugetdesc(desk, 2, 9) < 9 {
        give 2
    }
    let total = desk[d + 2] + desk[d + 3] * 256
    if total < 9 {
        give 2
    }
    if total > 2048 {
        give 2
    }
    if ugetdesc(desk, 2, total) < total {
        give 2
    }
    let cfgval = desk[d + 5]
    // The arrangement's walk: a mass-storage face and
    // its two bulk doors, as the keyboard's waking
    // walks for its one door.
    let off = 0
    let instick = 0
    let ifnum = 0
    let epin = 0
    let epinmax = 0
    let epout = 0
    let epoutmax = 0
    while off + 2 <= total {
        let len = desk[d + off]
        let kind = desk[d + off + 1]
        if len < 2 {
            off = total + 1
        } else {
            if kind == 4 {
                if len >= 9 {
                    let match = 0
                    if desk[d + off + 5] == 8 {
                        if desk[d + off + 6] == 6 {
                            if desk[d + off + 7] == 80 {
                                match = 1
                            }
                        }
                    }
                    instick = match
                    if match == 1 {
                        ifnum = desk[d + off + 2]
                    }
                }
            }
            if kind == 5 {
                if instick == 1 {
                    if len >= 7 {
                        let attr = desk[d + off + 3]
                        if attr - (attr / 4) * 4 == 2 {
                            let door = desk[d + off + 2]
                            let bound = desk[d + off + 4] + desk[d + off + 5] * 256
                            if door >= 128 {
                                epin = door - (door / 16) * 16
                                epinmax = bound
                            } else {
                                epout = door - (door / 16) * 16
                                epoutmax = bound
                            }
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
            off = off + len
        }
    }
    if epin == 0 {
        give 3
    }
    if epout == 0 {
        give 3
    }
    sp(desk, 20, epin)
    sp(desk, 24, epinmax)
    sp(desk, 28, epin * 2 + 1)
    sp(desk, 32, epout)
    sp(desk, 36, epoutmax)
    sp(desk, 40, epout * 2)
    // Arrange the two bulk doors with the controller:
    // the input carries the place's context copied
    // from the output the addressing laid, its door
    // count grown to the greater door's place, and
    // each door's own context — the out door's kind
    // reckoned 2, the in door's 6, in the controller's
    // reckoning of kinds (the +4 word: the error
    // allowance's 6, the kind at eight times itself,
    // the packet bound high).
    let inp = sg(desk, 76)
    let outp = sg(desk, 80)
    let cs = get32(desk, 208)
    let dciin = sg(desk, 28)
    let dciout = sg(desk, 40)
    let dcimax = dciin
    if dciout > dcimax {
        dcimax = dciout
    }
    xzero(desk, inp, 4224)
    let ci = 0
    while ci < 32 {
        desk[inp + cs + ci] = desk[outp + ci]
        ci = ci + 1
    }
    let dw0 = get32(desk, inp + cs)
    put32(desk, inp + cs, dw0 - (dw0 / 268435456) * 268435456 + dcimax * 268435456)
    let addflags = 1
    let bit = 1
    let bi = 0
    while bi < dciout {
        bit = bit * 2
        bi = bi + 1
    }
    addflags = addflags + bit
    bit = 1
    bi = 0
    while bi < dciin {
        bit = bit * 2
        bi = bi + 1
    }
    addflags = addflags + bit
    put32(desk, inp + 4, addflags)
    let ooff = inp + cs * (1 + dciout)
    put32(desk, ooff, 0)
    put32(desk, ooff + 4, 6 + 16 + epoutmax * 65536)
    put32(desk, ooff + 8, xphys(desk, sg(desk, 88)) + 1)
    put32(desk, ooff + 16, 512)
    let ioff = inp + cs * (1 + dciin)
    put32(desk, ioff, 0)
    put32(desk, ioff + 4, 6 + 48 + epinmax * 65536)
    put32(desk, ioff + 8, xphys(desk, sg(desk, 92)) + 1)
    put32(desk, ioff + 16, 512)
    if xcmd(desk, 12, xphys(desk, inp), 0, sg(desk, 8)) != 1 {
        give 2
    }
    ustagesetup1(desk, 0, 9, cfgval)
    ustagesetup2(desk, 0, 0)
    if ucontrol(desk, 0, 1, 0) < 0 {
        give 2
    }
    usbwait(1)
    give 4
}

// ---- the bulk-only transport ----

// Carries one command the transport's way: the
// command's own bytes stand staged by the caller in
// the command's room (the data ground's +5120), with
// its length; the wrapper goes out on the bulk-out
// ring (its mark growing, its direction and length
// told), the data crosses on its own door when there
// is data, and the status wrapper comes back on the
// bulk-in ring and is read — its signature checked
// and its standing given back: 0 the command passed,
// 1 it failed (the device answered and refused), -1
// the carriage itself did not complete.
make ubotgo(desk: bytes, inward: number, datalen: number, cdblen: number) -> number {
    let d = sg(desk, 96)
    let cbw = d + 4096
    let csw = d + 4608
    let cdb = d + 5120
    let tag = sg(desk, 48) + 1
    sp(desk, 48, tag)
    put32(desk, cbw, 1128420181)
    put32(desk, cbw + 4, tag)
    put32(desk, cbw + 8, datalen)
    if inward == 1 {
        desk[cbw + 12] = 128
    } else {
        desk[cbw + 12] = 0
    }
    desk[cbw + 13] = 0
    desk[cbw + 14] = cdblen
    let ci = 0
    while ci < 16 {
        desk[cbw + 15 + ci] = desk[cdb + ci]
        ci = ci + 1
    }
    ustage(desk, xphys(desk, cbw), 0, 31, 1024 + 32)
    uenq(desk, sg(desk, 88), 60, 64)
    xbell(desk, sg(desk, 8), sg(desk, 40))
    if uwaitep(desk, sg(desk, 40)) != 1 {
        give 0 - 1
    }
    if datalen > 0 {
        if inward == 1 {
            ustage(desk, xphys(desk, d), 0, datalen, 1024 + 32)
            uenq(desk, sg(desk, 92), 68, 72)
            xbell(desk, sg(desk, 8), sg(desk, 28))
            if uwaitep(desk, sg(desk, 28)) != 1 {
                give 0 - 1
            }
        } else {
            ustage(desk, xphys(desk, d), 0, datalen, 1024 + 32)
            uenq(desk, sg(desk, 88), 60, 64)
            xbell(desk, sg(desk, 8), sg(desk, 40))
            if uwaitep(desk, sg(desk, 40)) != 1 {
                give 0 - 1
            }
        }
    }
    ustage(desk, xphys(desk, csw), 0, 13, 1024 + 32)
    uenq(desk, sg(desk, 92), 68, 72)
    xbell(desk, sg(desk, 8), sg(desk, 28))
    if uwaitep(desk, sg(desk, 28)) != 1 {
        give 0 - 1
    }
    if get32(desk, csw) != 1396855637 {
        give 0 - 1
    }
    give desk[csw + 12]
}

// Zeroes the command's room: each command below then
// lays its own bytes there by hand, the big-endian
// way the SCSI words ask, each in its own making so
// the laying stands plain to read.
make ucbdzero(desk: bytes) {
    let cdb = sg(desk, 96) + 5120
    let i = 0
    while i < 16 {
        desk[cdb + i] = 0
        i = i + 1
    }
}

// Asks whether the stick stands ready (TEST UNIT
// READY), hearing a refusal the device's own way:
// when the command fails, its sense is asked for
// (REQUEST SENSE) and the asking made once more, as
// the transport prescribes for a device still
// settling. Gives back 1 when the stick stands
// ready, 0 when it does not.
make utestready(desk: bytes) -> number {
    let cdb = sg(desk, 96) + 5120
    ucbdzero(desk)
    desk[cdb] = 0
    let st = ubotgo(desk, 0, 0, 6)
    if st == 0 {
        give 1
    }
    if st != 1 {
        give 0
    }
    ucbdzero(desk)
    desk[cdb] = 3
    desk[cdb + 4] = 18
    if ubotgo(desk, 1, 18, 6) != 0 {
        give 0
    }
    ucbdzero(desk)
    desk[cdb] = 0
    if ubotgo(desk, 0, 0, 6) == 0 {
        give 1
    }
    give 0
}

// Reads the stick's measure (READ CAPACITY): its
// last sector's number and its sector's length, the
// big-endian way. A stick whose sector is not 512
// bytes cannot carry this system's keeping, and the
// raising refuses it. Gives back the sector count,
// or 0 when the asking failed.
make ucapacity(desk: bytes) -> number {
    let d = sg(desk, 96)
    let cdb = d + 5120
    ucbdzero(desk)
    desk[cdb] = 37
    if ubotgo(desk, 1, 8, 10) != 0 {
        give 0
    }
    let last = desk[d] * 16777216 + desk[d + 1] * 65536 + desk[d + 2] * 256 + desk[d + 3]
    let size = desk[d + 4] * 16777216 + desk[d + 5] * 65536 + desk[d + 6] * 256 + desk[d + 7]
    if size != 512 {
        give 0
    }
    give last + 1
}

// Reads one sector of the stick into the given block
// (READ(10), one sector, the sector's number laid
// big-endian in the command). Gives back 1 when the
// sector truly came, 0 when it did not.
make uread(desk: bytes, sector: number, block: bytes) -> number {
    let d = sg(desk, 96)
    let cdb = d + 5120
    ucbdzero(desk)
    desk[cdb] = 40
    desk[cdb + 2] = andmask(sector / 16777216, 255)
    desk[cdb + 3] = andmask(sector / 65536, 255)
    desk[cdb + 4] = andmask(sector / 256, 255)
    desk[cdb + 5] = andmask(sector, 255)
    desk[cdb + 8] = 1
    if ubotgo(desk, 1, 512, 10) != 0 {
        give 0
    }
    let i = 0
    while i < 512 {
        block[i] = desk[d + i]
        i = i + 1
    }
    give 1
}

// Writes one sector of the stick from the given block
// (WRITE(10), one sector). Gives back 1 when the
// sector was truly written, 0 when it was not.
make uwrite(desk: bytes, sector: number, block: bytes) -> number {
    let d = sg(desk, 96)
    let cdb = d + 5120
    let i = 0
    while i < 512 {
        desk[d + i] = block[i]
        i = i + 1
    }
    ucbdzero(desk)
    desk[cdb] = 42
    desk[cdb + 2] = andmask(sector / 16777216, 255)
    desk[cdb + 3] = andmask(sector / 65536, 255)
    desk[cdb + 4] = andmask(sector / 256, 255)
    desk[cdb + 5] = andmask(sector, 255)
    desk[cdb + 8] = 1
    if ubotgo(desk, 0, 512, 10) != 0 {
        give 0
    }
    give 1
}

// How many sectors the stick holds, once raised: the
// ledger's own reckoning, 0 before any raising.
make usectors(desk: bytes) -> number {
    if get32(desk, 252) != 0 {
        if sg(desk, 0) == 1 {
            give sg(desk, 44)
        }
    }
    give 0
}

// Commits what the stick itself may still hold
// (SYNCHRONIZE CACHE), as ataflush commits a hard
// disk's cache before the resting. Gives back 1 when
// the word was carried to a raised stick, 0 when
// there is none.
make uflush(desk: bytes) -> number {
    if usectors(desk) > 0 {
        let cdb = sg(desk, 96) + 5120
        ucbdzero(desk)
        desk[cdb] = 53
        if ubotgo(desk, 0, 0, 10) == 0 {
            give 1
        }
    }
    give 0
}

// Raises the stick, whole: when the xHCI controller
// stands walking (its road's ledger says so), the
// ports are walked as its own raising walked them —
// a device standing on a port is reset and woken —
// with the keyboard's own port skipped by number, and
// the two ledger places the walk borrows from the
// keyboard road (its port, its speed) handed back as
// they were found. The first device that wakes as a
// stick is asked its readiness and its measure, and
// the walk ends. Gives back the stick's sector count,
// or 0 when no stick stands raised: no controller, no
// device, a device of another kind on every port, or
// a stick that would not answer — each told apart in
// the stick ledger's standing (2 when the bus simply
// holds no stick, 255 when one answered and failed).
make ustart(desk: bytes) -> number {
    if get32(desk, 252) != 0 {
        if sg(desk, 0) == 1 {
            give sg(desk, 44)
        }
    }
    let xst = get32(desk, 4)
    if xst != 1 {
        if xst != 2 {
            give 0
        }
    }
    ubuild(desk)
    sp(desk, 0, 2)
    let saveport = get32(desk, 8)
    let savespeed = get32(desk, 12)
    let kbport = 0
    if xst == 2 {
        kbport = saveport
    }
    let op = get32(desk, 104)
    let p = 1
    let answer = 0
    while p <= get32(desk, 116) {
        if answer == 0 {
            if p != kbport {
                let poff = op + 1024 + (p - 1) * 16
                if andmask(xmread(desk, poff), 1) != 0 {
                    sp(desk, 4, p)
                    if xresetport(desk, p) == 1 {
                        sp(desk, 12, get32(desk, 12))
                        let woke = uwake(desk)
                        if woke == 4 {
                            if utestready(desk) == 1 {
                                let cap = ucapacity(desk)
                                if cap > 0 {
                                    sp(desk, 44, cap)
                                    sp(desk, 0, 1)
                                    answer = cap
                                } else {
                                    sp(desk, 0, 255)
                                }
                            } else {
                                sp(desk, 0, 255)
                            }
                        }
                        if woke == 2 {
                            sp(desk, 0, 255)
                        }
                        if woke != 4 {
                            // A candidate this road woke but
                            // cannot keep is set down again,
                            // its claim given back (the
                            // Disable Slot command, number
                            // 10), so the device stands as it
                            // stood before the asking.
                            if sg(desk, 8) >= 1 {
                                let freed = xcmd(desk, 10, 0, 0, sg(desk, 8))
                            }
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        }
        p = p + 1
    }
    put32(desk, 8, saveport)
    put32(desk, 12, savespeed)
    give answer
}

// ---- the keeping, on the stick ----
//
// The second half of this library: diskkeep.nifla's
// layout kept on the stick, word for word — the card
// at sector 8, the notes page's header at sector 64
// and its notes from sector 65, the picture's header
// at sector 80 and its three sectors after — with the
// one difference the transport asks: every reading
// and writing rides uread and uwrite above, and a
// reading that does not come is the twin of a disk
// that is not there. Each making mirrors its
// diskkeep fellow's words, so the two tellings can be
// read against each other.

// The card's stored byte, from the stick (the offset
// with 64 added), or 0 when there is no card — or no
// stick — to read.
make usavedoffset(desk: bytes) -> number {
    if usectors(desk) > 0 {
        let block = makebytes(512)
        if uread(desk, 8, block) == 1 {
            if block[0] == 67 {
                if block[1] == 78 {
                    give block[2]
                }
            }
        }
    }
    give 0
}

// The card's chime byte, from the stick: 1 on, 2 off,
// 0 no card to read (diskkeep's savedchime tells the
// standing whole).
make usavedchime(desk: bytes) -> number {
    if usectors(desk) > 0 {
        let block = makebytes(512)
        if uread(desk, 8, block) == 1 {
            if block[0] == 67 {
                if block[1] == 78 {
                    give block[3]
                }
            }
        }
    }
    give 0
}

// The card's size byte, from the stick: 1 usual, 2
// large, 0 no card to read.
make usavedsize(desk: bytes) -> number {
    if usectors(desk) > 0 {
        let block = makebytes(512)
        if uread(desk, 8, block) == 1 {
            if block[0] == 67 {
                if block[1] == 78 {
                    give block[4]
                }
            }
        }
    }
    give 0
}

// Writes the card whole to the stick: the given
// offset, chime byte, and size byte. Gives back 1
// when the choices were truly written, 0 when there
// is no stick to remember them on, or the writing
// did not stand.
make urememberall(desk: bytes, offset: number, chime: number, size: number) -> number {
    if usectors(desk) > 0 {
        let block = makebytes(512)
        block[0] = 67
        block[1] = 78
        block[2] = offset + 64
        block[3] = chime
        block[4] = size
        give uwrite(desk, 8, block)
    }
    give 0
}

// Writes the card for the given offset to the stick,
// keeping whatever chime and size choices the card
// already carries.
make uremember(desk: bytes, offset: number) -> number {
    give urememberall(desk, offset, usavedchime(desk), usavedsize(desk))
}

// Reads the kept notes from the stick into the main
// body's notes block, as notesload reads them from a
// hard disk. Gives back how many notes stand kept.
make unotesload(desk: bytes, block: bytes) -> number {
    if usectors(desk) > 0 {
        let head = makebytes(512)
        if uread(desk, 64, head) == 1 {
            if head[0] == 67 {
                if head[1] == 78 {
                    if head[2] == 78 {
                        let count = head[3]
                        if count > 8 {
                            count = 8
                        }
                        let sector = makebytes(512)
                        let i = 0
                        let whole = 1
                        while i < count {
                            if uread(desk, 65 + i, sector) == 1 {
                                let j = 0
                                while j < 64 {
                                    block[i * 64 + j] = sector[j]
                                    j = j + 1
                                }
                            } else {
                                whole = 0
                            }
                            i = i + 1
                        }
                        if whole == 1 {
                            give count
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
    give 0
}

// Writes the notes block's kept notes to the stick:
// the header first, then one sector to a note. Gives
// back 1 when the page was written whole, 0 when it
// was not.
make unotesave(desk: bytes, block: bytes, count: number) -> number {
    if usectors(desk) > 0 {
        let head = makebytes(512)
        head[0] = 67
        head[1] = 78
        head[2] = 78
        head[3] = count
        if uwrite(desk, 64, head) != 1 {
            give 0
        }
        let i = 0
        while i < count {
            let sector = makebytes(512)
            let j = 0
            while j < 64 {
                sector[j] = block[i * 64 + j]
                j = j + 1
            }
            if uwrite(desk, 65 + i, sector) != 1 {
                give 0
            }
            i = i + 1
        }
        give 1
    }
    give 0
}

// Reads the kept picture from the stick into the
// main body's picture block, as picload reads it from
// a hard disk. Gives back the kept chosen-color
// figure when a picture stands kept, 0 when none
// does, or there is no stick to read.
make upicload(desk: bytes, block: bytes) -> number {
    if usectors(desk) > 0 {
        let head = makebytes(512)
        if uread(desk, 80, head) == 1 {
            if head[0] == 67 {
                if head[1] == 78 {
                    if head[2] == 80 {
                        if head[3] == 1 {
                            let sector = makebytes(512)
                            let s = 0
                            let whole = 1
                            while s < 3 {
                                if uread(desk, 81 + s, sector) == 1 {
                                    let j = 0
                                    while j < 512 {
                                        let at = s * 512 + j
                                        if at < 1144 {
                                            block[at] = sector[j]
                                        }
                                        j = j + 1
                                    }
                                } else {
                                    whole = 0
                                }
                                s = s + 1
                            }
                            if whole == 1 {
                                let sel = head[4]
                                if sel < 48 {
                                    sel = 48
                                }
                                if sel > 53 {
                                    sel = 48
                                }
                                give sel
                            }
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
    give 0
}

// Reads the kept picture's name from the stick into
// the given block at the given place, as picnameload
// reads it from a hard disk. Gives back the name's
// length.
make upicnameload(desk: bytes, block: bytes, off: number) -> number {
    block[off] = 0
    if usectors(desk) > 0 {
        let head = makebytes(512)
        if uread(desk, 80, head) == 1 {
            if head[0] == 67 {
                if head[1] == 78 {
                    if head[2] == 80 {
                        if head[3] == 1 {
                            let len = head[5]
                            if len > 43 {
                                len = 43
                            }
                            let i = 0
                            while i < len {
                                block[off + 1 + i] = head[6 + i]
                                i = i + 1
                            }
                            block[off] = len
                            give len
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
    give 0
}

// Writes the picture's header to the stick, as
// picsave's first writing does to a hard disk: the
// kept byte, the chosen-color figure, and — when a
// picture stands kept — the name carried from the
// given name block's place 640. (The twin stands in
// two makings, header and body, where picsave stands
// in one: a call can carry six words, and the desk
// and the two blocks and the two figures would make
// eight.) Gives back 1 when the header was written,
// 0 when it was not.
make upichead(desk: bytes, present: number, sel: number, nameblock: bytes) -> number {
    if usectors(desk) > 0 {
        let head = makebytes(512)
        head[0] = 67
        head[1] = 78
        head[2] = 80
        head[3] = present
        head[4] = sel
        if present == 1 {
            let nlen = nameblock[640]
            if nlen > 43 {
                nlen = 43
            }
            head[5] = nlen
            let ni = 0
            while ni < nlen {
                head[6 + ni] = nameblock[640 + 1 + ni]
                ni = ni + 1
            }
        }
        give uwrite(desk, 80, head)
    }
    give 0
}

// Writes the picture block's painted region to the
// stick: the three picture sectors, each holding its
// stretch of the block, as picsave's second writing
// lays them on a hard disk. Gives back 1 when all
// three were written, 0 when any was not.
make upicbody(desk: bytes, block: bytes) -> number {
    if usectors(desk) > 0 {
        let s = 0
        while s < 3 {
            let sector = makebytes(512)
            let j = 0
            while j < 512 {
                let at = s * 512 + j
                if at < 1144 {
                    sector[j] = block[at]
                }
                j = j + 1
            }
            if uwrite(desk, 81 + s, sector) != 1 {
                give 0
            }
            s = s + 1
        }
        give 1
    }
    give 0
}

// Gives the stick over to the system's keeping, as
// disksetup gives a hard disk: the stick's first
// sixty-four sectors wiped to zeros, the card written
// last of all, and the card read back — only a card
// that truly stands earns a 1.
make udisksetup(desk: bytes, offset: number, chime: number, size: number) -> number {
    if usectors(desk) > 0 {
        let block = makebytes(512)
        let sector = 0
        let whole = 1
        while sector < 64 {
            if uwrite(desk, sector, block) != 1 {
                whole = 0
            }
            sector = sector + 1
        }
        if whole == 1 {
            block[0] = 67
            block[1] = 78
            block[2] = offset + 64
            block[3] = chime
            block[4] = size
            if uwrite(desk, 8, block) == 1 {
                let back = makebytes(512)
                if uread(desk, 8, back) == 1 {
                    if back[0] == 67 {
                        if back[1] == 78 {
                            if back[2] == offset + 64 {
                                give 1
                            }
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
    give 0
}

// ---- the system itself, from the stick (Stone 50) ----

// Whether the stick carries the system, and how long
// its image runs: the stick's first sector is the
// system's own master boot record (Stone 17) — its
// signature stands at the sector's last two bytes,
// and its partition table's first entry spans the
// image, its count being the image's length in
// sectors — and the image's volume descriptor stands
// at its sixty-fourth sector with its mark (a first
// byte of 1, then the letters CD001, as the doorman
// reads it). Gives back the image's length in
// sectors when the stick carries the system whole —
// the length sane (a thousand sectors at least, and
// no more than the stick holds) — and 0 when it does
// not: no stick raised, a blank stick, or a stick
// carrying only a keeping (Stone 43's ground, whose
// first sector stands empty and whose sixty-fourth
// carries the notes page's header, not this mark).
make ustickimage(desk: bytes) -> number {
    if usectors(desk) > 0 {
        let block = makebytes(512)
        if uread(desk, 0, block) == 1 {
            if block[510] == 85 {
                if block[511] == 170 {
                    let count = block[458] + block[459] * 256 + block[460] * 65536 + block[461] * 16777216
                    if count >= 1000 {
                        if count <= usectors(desk) {
                            if uread(desk, 64, block) == 1 {
                                if block[0] == 1 {
                                    if block[1] == 67 {
                                        if block[2] == 68 {
                                            if block[3] == 48 {
                                                if block[4] == 48 {
                                                    if block[5] == 49 {
                                                        give count
                                                    }
                                                }
                                            }
                                        }
                                    }
                                }
                            }
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
    give 0
}

// Copies the stick's system image onto the hard disk,
// sector by sector, from the stick's first sector to
// the disk's sector at the given beginning, through
// the given block: each sector read from the stick
// and written to the disk before the next is read, so
// the stick's bytes are never held in more than the
// one sector in flight. Gives back how many sectors
// were copied whole: the image's whole length when
// the copy finished, or the count standing when a
// reading of the stick failed — the copy stops there,
// and what stands on the disk is a part of an image
// that nothing yet points at (the disk's boot record
// is laid only after a whole, proved copy; see
// ulayrecord below), so a copy that did not finish
// leaves the disk exactly as bootable, or as
// unbootable, as it stood before. (A writing to the
// disk that fails stops the machine, as every writing
// through the language's disk word may — the disk
// library's standing law, not this making's choice.)
make ucopyimage(desk: bytes, base: number, count: number, block: bytes) -> number {
    let i = 0
    while i < count {
        if uread(desk, i, block) != 1 {
            give i
        }
        let w = diskwrite(base + i, block)
        i = i + 1
    }
    give count
}

// Proves a copied image at three of its places: the
// volume descriptor's sector (the image's
// sixty-fourth), the sector after it where the disc's
// own directory ground stands (its eightieth), and
// the image's last sector — each read from the disk
// and from the stick, and compared byte for byte
// through the given block and one of the making's
// own (a call can carry only so many words, and two
// blocks handed in beside the desk would overflow
// it). Gives back 1 when all three places stand
// identical, 0 when any reading failed or any byte
// differs: a copy that does not prove is not an
// installed system, and the main body says so
// plainly and lays no boot record for it.
make ucopyproof(desk: bytes, base: number, count: number, block: bytes) -> number {
    let other = makebytes(512)
    let places = 0
    while places < 3 {
        let at = 64
        if places == 1 {
            at = 80
        }
        if places == 2 {
            at = count - 1
        }
        if uread(desk, at, block) != 1 {
            give 0
        }
        selectdrive()
        let r = diskread(base + at, other)
        let i = 0
        let same = 1
        while i < 512 {
            if block[i] != other[i] {
                same = 0
            }
            i = i + 1
        }
        if same == 0 {
            give 0
        }
        places = places + 1
    }
    give 1
}

// Lays the hard disk's own master boot record, last
// of all in an installing: the stick's first sector —
// Cardnull's own record (Stone 17), whose stub now
// reads where its image begins from the record's own
// table — with that table's beginning set to the
// given sector, where the copied image stands on this
// disk; the span the table names is the stick's own,
// the image's length, and stands as it was read. The
// record is then read back from the disk and compared
// byte for byte through a block of the making's own,
// for the carrying limit the proof above tells.
// Gives back 1 when the record stands on the disk
// exactly as laid, 0 when the stick's record could
// not be read or the disk's does not match — and the
// installing is then not claimed, as every step of it
// is proved or plainly refused.
make ulayrecord(desk: bytes, base: number, block: bytes) -> number {
    let other = makebytes(512)
    if uread(desk, 0, block) != 1 {
        give 0
    }
    block[454] = lobyte(base)
    block[455] = hibyte(base)
    block[456] = lobyte(base / 65536)
    block[457] = hibyte(base / 65536)
    selectdrive()
    let w = diskwrite(0, block)
    let r = diskread(0, other)
    let i = 0
    let same = 1
    while i < 512 {
        if block[i] != other[i] {
            same = 0
        }
        i = i + 1
    }
    give same
}
